\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1\cf0 .    Lord, go with me into the garden
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  so we could go and pray there
\par  Please to your side let me also kneel
\par  do not let me ever leave you
\par  You are the only good teacher
\par   I will learn how to pray from you.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. You went there in fear and with swiftness
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  to meditate on your suffering
\par  it is then necessary that
\par  I should be mindful of this
\par  so that whenever I am praying
\par  I will be sorry for my sins.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.   You withdrew quietly some where
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0   where it was very quiet and serene
\par  that is the same that I should do
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 quiet and solemn in my life
\par and leave the world for a while
\par and you and me live for a while.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  You are the father's beloved son
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Your name is Abba Father
\par I wish your father is mine also
\par A father's love does not falter,
\par Let me hold on fast onto you
\par please respond when I call on you.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  O Father teach me how to pray
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 as you are used to do often
\par Allow me to shift all my problems
\par onto you my Lord and my king
\par Give ears to me when'er I call
\par \pard         allow me to come close to you.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

